# Orchestration

For non-trivial work in this repo, follow `.cursor/skills/using-cc-skills/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/skills/lead-engineer/SKILL.md`.

## Routing (summary)

| Situation | Skill |
|-----------|--------|
| Feature / multi-file / unclear scope | `lead-engineer` |
| Implement one vertical slice | `senior-engineer` (+ `rust-backend-engineer` or `frontend-engineer`) |
| UI/IA/states/a11y | `ui-ux-engineer` |
| After implementation | `code-review-quality` then `qa-engineer` |
| New behavior / bugfix | `tdd-workflow` |
| About to claim done | `verification-loop` |
| Auth, money, input, secrets | `security-review` |
| New/changed HTTP endpoints | `api-contract-design` |
| Replicate one flow from another app | `feature-recon` → `feature-adapt`; after the build, `feature-parity` |

## Hard gates

- Lead does **not** implement non-trivial feature code; delegates via Task subagents.
- QA must **not** be the author of the code under test.
- No sign-off without pasted verification evidence.
- Small fixes (typo, one-file config): implement directly; still verify.
